        "text": "<|message_model|><|content_thinking|>The user wants a Python implementation of a bounded LRU cache with get and put methods. Requirements:\n- Use collections.OrderedDict\n- Reject non-positive capacity\n- Include four small unittest cases\n- Return complete Python file\n\nNeed produce final answer with complete Python file. Need ensure correctness.\n\nDesign:\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nimport unittest\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity):\n        if not isinstance(capacity, int) or isinstance(capacity, bool) or capacity <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"capacity must be a positive integer\")\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self._cache = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        if key not in self._cache:\n            return None\n        self._cache.move_to_end(key)\n        return self._cache[key]\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        if key in self._cache:\n            self._cache.move_to_end(key)\n            self",
